Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:17:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(analysis): NASA POWER historical analysis with D3.js
 charts

Rebuild the Historical analysis panel around NASA POWER (plus Open-Meteo
ERA5) with research-based statistics and D3.js visualisations.

Analysis core (src/lib/analysis):
- POWER live catalog (daily 150 / monthly 1388 params), point, monthly
  regional fetch with cache and queue; Open-Meteo adapter; ERA5 pairs
  with unit conversion.
- Aggregation by kind (mean / rate / count / circular) with 80% monthly
  completeness; annual trends only.
- OLS with Santer et al. (2000) autocorrelation-adjusted p, Mann-Kendall
  and Sen's slope, Pettitt change-point, ETCCDI-style p90/p10 exceedance,
  distribution shift, POWER vs ERA5 comparison, LTTB downsampling.
- Thematic parameter grouping (powerTheme) after the C3S Climate Atlas.

UI (historical-panel + components/analysis):
- Tabs: Overview, Series, Seasonal, Anomaly, Distribution, Compare,
  Spatial (POWER regional grid, optional map overlay).
- Overview: plain-language insight, KPI tiles with sparklines, climate
  stripes, baseline shading, value-labelled legends.
- Accessible WAI-ARIA combobox parameter picker and ARIA tabs.
- Okabe-Ito categorical colours; IPCC-style diverging/sequential
  palettes (no rainbow maps); SVG and CSV export; dark mode.

Fixes: Math.min/max stack overflow on long series, over-confident daily
OLS p-values, arithmetic mean of wind direction, precipitation totals,
panel not loading on open.

Tests: analysis-stats and analysis-sources suites (387 tests passing).
Docs: ANALYSIS-D3-POWER-BN.md and screenshots in docs/analysis-ui/.
